---
args: {"inbox": "ExperienceInbox", "studyState": "ExperienceStudyState | null"}
returns: "ExperienceInvestigation"
---
1. Bind prior to studyState or ExperienceStudyState { revision: 0, episodes: [], associations: [], mechanisms: [], trials: [], outcomes: [], removals: [], clinicalRoutingReceiptIds: [] }. Bind removals to removeAttributableDerivatives(inbox.changes, prior, inbox.governance) when changed feedback contains an authorized consent withdrawal, otherwise to []. Exclude the affected sources and attributable derivatives from any new public findings before continuing. Preserve only permitted restricted audit references and actual removal receipts.
2. Bind episodes = separateAdministrativeEpisodes(inbox.feedback, inbox.changes, inbox.governance). Route clinical concerns through the supplied clinical process using only the necessary restricted information. A pending routing intention is not a triage receipt; do not interpret symptoms, diagnose, or claim the clinical concern was handled.
3. Bind associations = linkAuthorizedJourneys(episodes, inbox.feedback, inbox.governance). Link only within established authorized patient scope and time windows. Repeated reports of one episode remain one experience; an ambiguous link cannot expose another person's record.
4. Bind mechanisms = investigateRivalMechanisms(episodes, associations, prior.mechanisms). Keep administrative mechanisms provisional with contrary cases and a discriminating next observation. Bind trials = designAdministrativeTrials(mechanisms, inbox.governance, prior.trials), preserving ongoing approved trial identities and actual implementation evidence. If no actual outcome metrics exist, keep outcomes to prior supported outcomes and continue to the complete state return with the trials’ evidence-collection work; do not invent results.
5. For each trial with actual supplied metrics call adjudicateAdministrativeOutcome(trial, itsMetrics, episodes, associations), collecting the returned outcomes. Preserve severe minority barriers and downstream team burden even if aggregate access appears better.
6. Bind nextStudy as ExperienceStudyState { revision: advance only for new permitted source, trial, outcome or removal facts, episodes: permitted current episodes plus unaffected prior episodes, associations: only currently authorized links plus unaffected permitted prior links, mechanisms: actual revised mechanisms retaining counterevidence, trials, outcomes: prior supported outcomes plus actual new outcomes by trial/metric identity, removals: prior.removals plus current removals merged once, clinicalRoutingReceiptIds: prior IDs plus only actual matching authorized routing receipts }. Keep restricted withdrawal audit references separate from public text. Return ExperienceInvestigation { studyState: nextStudy, administrativeFindings: supported administrative findings excluding withdrawn attribution, pendingClinicalRoutes: unresolved routing intentions without actual receipts, nextObservations: the trials’ actual discriminating observation needs, outcomeDecisions: newly supported or inconclusive outcomes, consentActions: removals, studyLimits: missing frame/metrics, uncertainty and downstream burden }. Neither fewer complaints nor an administrative change establishes clinical benefit.
